Question: Implement an AWS Lambda function using Node.js that listens for S3 bucket events (e.g., object creation) and triggers an email notification via Amazon Simple Email Service (SES) whenever a new file is uploaded.
PLAINFORMAT

<think>// Import required AWS SDK clients and commands for Node.js
const AWS = require('aws-sdk');
const { S3 } = require('@aws-sdk/client-s3');
const s3Client = new S3();
const ses = new AWS.SES();

exports.handler = async (event) => {
    // Get the object key and bucket name from the event
    const objectKey = event.Records[0].s3.object.key;
    const bucketName = event.Records[0].s3.bucket.name;

    try {
        // Retrieve the object's metadata
        const params = {
            Bucket: bucketName,
            Key: objectKey
        };
        const metadata = await s3Client.headObject(params).promise();

        // Send email notification
        const emailParams = {
            Source: 'your-verified-email@example.com',
            Destination: {
                ToAddresses: ['recipient@example.com']
            },
            Message: {
                Subject: {
                    Data: 'New File Uploaded'
                },
                Body: {
                    Text: {
                        Data: `A new file has been uploaded to ${bucketName}:\n\nFile Name: ${objectKey}\nSize: ${metadata.ContentLength} bytes`
                    }
                }
            }
        };

        await ses.sendEmail(emailParams).promise();
        console.log(`Email sent successfully for file: ${objectKey}`);
    } catch (error) {
        console.error(`Error processing file ${objectKey}:`, error);
        throw error;
    }
};</think>

Question: In the circle with center $Q$, radii $AQ$ and $BQ$ form a right angle. The two smaller regions are tangent semicircles, as shown. The radius of the circle with center $Q$ is 14 inches. What is the radius of the smaller semicircle? Express your answer as a common fraction.

