<think>Since $\angle ACT=\angle ATC$ and $\angle CAT=36^\circ$, we have $2(\angle ATC) =180^\circ-36^\circ =144^\circ$ and $\angle
ATC=\angle ACT=72^\circ$. Because $\overline{TR}$ bisects $\angle
ATC$, $\angle CTR=\frac{1}{2}(72^\circ)=36^\circ$. In triangle $CRT$, $\angle CRT=180^\circ-36^\circ-72^\circ=72^\circ$.</think>

